    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Counting rules and scope",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 15
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### What these totals mean\\n\\n- A completed pipeline is one unique repository and pipeline number created inside the configured trial interval, with at least one workflow assigned to the selected worker. A mixed-host pipeline is counted once.\\n- Worker workflow executions count the worker's workflows, not pipeline steps. Cost per worker workflow divides the full-trial spend by these executions. Pipeline cost ratios divide by unique pipelines.\\n- Totals come from the exporter's persistent ledger and are exported as current gauges, so the counts remain available after Prometheus sample retention expires. The daily activity panel groups those current totals by pipeline creation day.\\n- Standalone Buildx calls, Fleet Runner jobs, and CI workflows run only on other hosts are excluded. Historical coverage must read `1` before using the cost ratios. This is CI cost accounting, not a count of container images or successful releases."
      }
    },
